From 608126a521dbf25b8f40ef567e491889f529eadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:33:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(adaptive): close the entry orbit exactly on its start

The HSM plan orbits the entry from its start and leaves the orbit where
it closed. adaptive::rings::circle computed the closing vertex at
a0 + TAU, an ulp off the start, and the plan's crossing law (orientation
predicate) read the spiral's first chord out of it as a proper crossing
of the orbit's first chord: the level was refused and cut with Offset
rings. That is why the user's STEP bore lost its HSM plan on Z 20 (since
#850) and Z 10 (since #839's finer mesh reshuffled the float noise).

The circle now closes exactly - its last point is its first, and the
start itself where the start lies on the circle (within 1e-9 mm). The
crossing law is unchanged.

Pinned by motion adaptive_orbit_seam (the dumped Z 10 center outline as
a 2-D pocket; crossed before the fix) and a rings unit test; the heavy
app pin is re-measured: no level falls back, 16197 / 15458 / 1581.

Fixes #980

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
